%% One message, end to end: from a gateway through the run loop and back (core/run.py, core/runtime.py).
%% The loop is explicit and boring on purpose (ADR 002): build context, call the model, run tools, repeat.
%% Every step publishes events; gateways render the events, never the model's messages (ADR 003).
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor You
  participant GW as Gateway (TUI / web / Telegram / REPL)
  participant App as Application
  participant RM as RunManager
  participant RT as AgentRuntime
  participant M as Main model
  participant TE as ToolExecutor + approvals
  participant S as Stores (transcript, SQLite)

  You->>GW: type a message (or /skill args)
  GW->>App: send_message(envelope)
  App->>App: budget check, expand /skill, drain monitor notes
  App->>RM: start(RunRequest)
  RM->>RT: run() under the per-session lock
  RT->>S: load the conversation
  Note over RT: events: run.started

  loop until the model answers without tool calls (or a limit stops it)
    RT->>RT: take queued messages (your follow-ups, monitor notes)
    alt context past 80% of the budget
      RT->>M: the input it was about to send + "summarise"
      M-->>RT: summary (saved as a marker, files in use attached)
      Note over RT: events: context.compacted, model.usage
    end
    RT->>RT: build context: system parts + summary + window
    RT->>M: ainvoke(context)
    M-->>RT: AI message (text and/or tool calls)
    Note over RT: events: model.usage, model.reasoning, assistant.message
    opt the message has tool calls
      RT->>TE: run the batch (in parallel)
      TE->>TE: gated? ask the rules, the classifier or you (diagram 04)
      TE-->>RT: tool results (big ones become artifacts)
      Note over RT: events: tool.started, tool.output, tool.completed
    end
  end

  RT->>S: append the run's messages, save the session
  Note over RT: events: run.completed (or run.failed)
  RT-->>RM: final answer
  RM-->>GW: event stream ends
  GW-->>You: answer, tool cards, cost
